CPA Key Billing — custom timezone/location extension

This work retains cpa-plugin-key-billing by Hao Wang, originally licensed
under the MIT License in LICENSE, at commit
4e405bd1d953cdc477cdbdd0d4890bec3b58abc3.
Source: https://github.com/haowang02/cpa-plugin-key-billing

The structured context matching and request-location alignment design in
internal/location/rewrite.go is adapted into Go from codex-proxy-rs:
backend/crates/providers/openai/src/transport/request.rs, commit
60570883007febebe732597a9881397098d724f5.
Source: https://github.com/zyycn/codex-proxy-rs
The original project is licensed under Apache License 2.0; the license is
reproduced in licenses/codex-proxy-rs-APACHE-2.0.txt. The adaptation uses Go
XML parsing and byte-preserving JSON field updates and adds conservative
message-type and malformed-metadata checks.

Modified files include location validation/normalization, per-credential
concurrency controls, timezone display, plugin registration and management
endpoints, independent diagnostics with read-only history import, the
management UI, and validation/build documentation. The customized version
removes the original billing, API Key, subscription, pricing, analytics,
request-event, and routing feature implementations.
No affiliation with or endorsement by the upstream maintainers is claimed.

Proxy configuration identity matching follows the MIT-licensed CLIProxyAPI StableIDGenerator and config synthesizer at commit ae3ee3be303fb07fb8173279923413005bf32177. The original license is included in licenses/CLIProxyAPI-MIT.txt.
